OL,2,W//%*// //%Q%**,-. *,$%**,%-,* %%**,! ,,
OL,3,GNEWSACommunity garden's food supply hit
OL,4,Aby dry summer
OL,5,
OL,6,FA community garden has been forced to
OL,7,Fthrow away food which was destined for
OL,8,Fthe local community as a result of
OL,9,Frecent dry weather.
OL,11,FVolunteers from NorthernLily CIC, a
OL,12,Fsocial enterprise in Oldham, said up to
OL,13,Fthree quarters of its plants, fruit and
OL,14,Fvegetables simply did not survive the
OL,15,Fhot summer, and the failed crops had to
OL,16,Fbe composted.
OL,18,F"Normally we grow over a tonne of food,
OL,19,Fwhich equates to 12,700 meals worth,
OL,20,Fand we give that away to our
OL,21,Fcommunity," said Victoria Holden.
OL,23,APub: 25-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NW Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
FL,410,400,260,160,0,100
